{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-1-kings-004",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 4,
  "title": "1 Kings 4",
  "display_title": "1 Kings 4",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "1-kings",
  "book": "1 Kings",
  "bookName": "1 Kings",
  "bookOrder": 11,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 4,
  "sortOrder": 11004,
  "verseCount": 34,
  "aliases": [
    "1 Kgs",
    "1Kgs",
    "1 Ki",
    "1Ki"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "So king Solomon was king over all Israel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "And these were the princes which he had; Azariah the son of Zadok the priest,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Elihoreph and Ahiah, the sons of Shisha, scribes; Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud, the recorder.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the host: and Zadok and Abiathar were the priests:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "And Azariah the son of Nathan was over the officers: and Zabud the son of Nathan was principal officer, and the king’s friend:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "And Ahishar was over the household: and Adoniram the son of Abda was over the tribute.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "And Solomon had twelve officers over all Israel, which provided victuals for the king and his household: each man his month in a year made provision.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "And these are their names: The son of Hur, in mount Ephraim:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "The son of Dekar, in Makaz, and in Shaalbim, and Bethshemesh, and Elonbethhanan:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "The son of Hesed, in Aruboth; to him pertained Sochoh, and all the land of Hepher:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "The son of Abinadab, in all the region of Dor; which had Taphath the daughter of Solomon to wife:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Baana the son of Ahilud; to him pertained Taanach and Megiddo, and all Bethshean, which is by Zartanah beneath Jezreel, from Bethshean to Abelmeholah, even unto the place that is beyond Jokneam:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "The son of Geber, in Ramothgilead; to him pertained the towns of Jair the son of Manasseh, which are in Gilead; to him also pertained the region of Argob, which is in Bashan, threescore great cities with walls and brasen bars:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Ahinadab the son of Iddo had Mahanaim:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Ahimaaz was in Naphtali; he also took Basmath the daughter of Solomon to wife:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Baanah the son of Hushai was in Asher and in Aloth:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Jehoshaphat the son of Paruah, in Issachar:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Shimei the son of Elah, in Benjamin:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Geber the son of Uri was in the country of Gilead, in the country of Sihon king of the Amorites, and of Og king of Bashan; and he was the only officer which was in the land.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Judah and Israel were many, as the sand which is by the sea in multitude, eating and drinking, and making merry.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "And Solomon reigned over all kingdoms from the river unto the land of the Philistines, and unto the border of Egypt: they brought presents, and served Solomon all the days of his life.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "And Solomon’s provision for one day was thirty measures of fine flour, and threescore measures of meal,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Ten fat oxen, and twenty oxen out of the pastures, and an hundred sheep, beside harts, and roebucks, and fallowdeer, and fatted fowl.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "For he had dominion over all the region on this side the river, from Tiphsah even to Azzah, over all the kings on this side the river: and he had peace on all sides round about him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "And Judah and Israel dwelt safely, every man under his vine and under his fig tree, from Dan even to Beersheba, all the days of Solomon.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "And Solomon had forty thousand stalls of horses for his chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "And those officers provided victual for king Solomon, and for all that came unto king Solomon’s table, every man in his month: they lacked nothing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Barley also and straw for the horses and dromedaries brought they unto the place where the officers were, every man according to his charge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "And God gave Solomon wisdom and understanding exceeding much, and largeness of heart, even as the sand that is on the sea shore.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "And Solomon’s wisdom excelled the wisdom of all the children of the east country, and all the wisdom of Egypt.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "For he was wiser than all men; than Ethan the Ezrahite, and Heman, and Chalcol, and Darda, the sons of Mahol: and his fame was in all nations round about.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "And he spake three thousand proverbs: and his songs were a thousand and five.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "And he spake of trees, from the cedar tree that is in Lebanon even unto the hyssop that springeth out of the wall: he spake also of beasts, and of fowl, and of creeping things, and of fishes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-kings:4:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "And there came of all people to hear the wisdom of Solomon, from all kings of the earth, which had heard of his wisdom.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Kings 4:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-kings:4:34"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
